    {
      "id": "stg_theory",
      "type": "lecture",
      "title": "Concept Download",
      "parts": [
        {
          "visual": "WELCOME TO ONIXLINGO.\n\nTo speak English, you need the 'Golden Formula':\nSubject (Actor) + Verb (Action) + Complement (Detail).",
          "audio": "Welcome. Let's master the code of English identity."
        },
        {
          "visual": "SINGULAR PRONOUNS:\n\nI (Yo)\nYou (Tú)\nHe (Él)\nShe (Ella)\nIt (Eso - para cosas/animales)",
          "audio": "First, the singular pronouns. I, You, He, She, and It."
        },
        {
          "visual": "PLURAL PRONOUNS:\n\nWe (Nosotros)\nYou (Ustedes - sí, es igual que Tú)\nThey (Ellos/Ellas)",
          "audio": "Now, the plurals. We, You, and They."
        },
        {
          "visual": "THE VERB 'TO BE' (Ser/Estar):\n\nI am\nYou are\nHe/She/It is\nWe/They are",
          "audio": "The verb To Be changes depending on the person. Am, Is, Are."
        },
        {
          "visual": "CONTRACTIONS (Short forms):\n\nI am -> I'm\nYou are -> You're\nHe is -> He's\nThey are -> They're",
          "audio": "Native speakers usually use contractions. Listen carefully."
        }
      ]
    },
